# Instructions

For state.checks.{{ name }} ONLY: find this source by its source_order; do not evaluate any other source in this packet.

Assess ONLY the physical text position of reference replacements in this source, not note meaning, targets, paragraph joins or missing OCR.

literal_edits describes edits from the original raw_text to analysed_text. Each original field was removed and each analysed field inserted at that location. A REF replacement must occupy the original printed marker position. An insertion of REF where the original contained no marker, combined with removing a marker elsewhere, does NOT preserve its position.

Check the literal edit operations and their original_before/original_after context. Inline math or Markdown escaping around the SAME marker can change; whitespace changes do not relocate a marker. If position is preserved, accept. If it demonstrably moved, reject. Insufficient evidence is not a demonstrable error.

# True

The replacements preserve original marker positions, or no displacement is established.

# False

A reference token demonstrably occupies a different position from its original marker.
